 "web": "These land on the same family at once. One household: the mother picks cardboard and plastic at the dump for a price she does not set; a teenage son is at the age when school starts to cost money and the dump starts to pay; the bus he would take to school crosses routes whose drivers pay to drive them; water comes by tank or truck on a schedule set by reservoir levels; an uncle in the U.S. sends money most months, and a cousin was just sent back; the lot the house stands on has no registered title, so when the roof leaks the only lender who says yes is the one who collects every day. No single barrier decided this family's life. Together they set the price.",
