   "plain": "To put a roof on before the rains, or restock a corner store (*pulpería*), a family needs a few thousand lempiras at once. Banks lend small amounts at about 20% a year to people with an ID, provable income and often a title. The state's micro-business line charges 22% a year, and only to registered businesses. Everyone else borrows from a lender who asks only for a signature, collects every day, and has charged about 20% a month. In the capital's markets, police have tied some of those lenders to the same groups that collect the war tax.",
