 "theology": {
  "readings": [
   "**Luke 10:25–37, the Good Samaritan.** The community carries its name. Read it slowly before the trip: a lawyer asks who is my neighbor? and Jesus answers with a story in which the despised outsider is the one who stops. He ends with a different question — who *became* a neighbor. Students arrive at Buen Samaritano and are tempted to cast themselves as the Samaritan. The text resists that.",
   "Stands on its own without the course."
  ],
  "question": "The people who work at the dump were here before I came and will be here after I leave. When I hand someone a meal and get back on the bus, which character in Luke 10 am I — and what would it take to become a neighbor rather than a visitor?"
 },
